================================================================================
WHAT THIS FILE IS
================================================================================

HearWrite's own code is MIT. It bundles no third party code and redistributes
no model weights: every model is downloaded, on demand, from its own publisher,
and verified against a SHA-256 pinned in src/hearwrite/models.py.

That means you inherit each model's terms directly from its publisher when you
choose to download it. This file records what those terms are, because "which
licence did that checkpoint have" is exactly the question nobody wants to answer
after shipping.

Two rules govern what may be added here, and both are enforced by tests:

  1. NOTHING GATED. No model may require an account, an access token, or a
     licence acceptance. A gated weight means a secret in CI and a file nobody
     can vendor, which breaks "clone it and run it".
  2. EVERY ENTRY RECORDS A LICENCE AND A CHECKSUM. No exceptions.

`hearwrite models` prints this information at runtime.


